==> provenance: full  (4/4 of decision ticket 14)
  [x] 1. Decided: artefact attestation vs reasoning-chain attestation (or both, with the seam).
        build ticket 89: twin/reproduce.py's _replay_subject is the seam, and it is no longer a score-card special case: both the `score` and `reliability` branches of replay() route their subject references through it, so reproducing a score card walks its bundle and reproducing a reliability diagram walks its score cards, each recursively — tests/test_reproduce.py::test_reproducing_a_reliability_diagram_walks_a_three_artefact_chain.
  [x] 2. An actor-identity model covering humans and agents, and what a signature asserts.
        build ticket 11: twin/sign.py — a human signature asserts accountability and binds to a role from a versioned register, never to an individual; an agent signature asserts reproducible origin and names what it does not assert. The two are non-interchangeable by type, and a human signature on a derived artefact is detected when the sidecar is read back.
